  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EXPLORE Phase 2: Forest Landscape Governance</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EXPLORE Phase 2: Forest Landscape Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of Explore is to support governments in using high quality research to improve policies and institutional frameworks for the inclusive and sustainable management of forest landscapes in Southeast Asia that contributes to the climate and development goals such as SDGs.

Phase 2 of Explore will lead to innovative and well designed and implemented research that is widely used by key stakeholders, including to support informed policy and decision making at landscape, national and regional levels. The specific objectives of the initiative are: 

- Regional, transboundary research projects are using participatory methods to develop and conduct high quality research on forest landscape governance in Southeast Asia

- Researchers are supporting informed policy making and implementation across the region

-Researchers of forest landscape governance in Southeast Asia have a stronger network with policy and decision makers at landscape, national, regional and international levels

- A member driven and inclusive forest landscape governance research network is fully functional

- The communication and knowledge strategy fosters visibility, awareness, engagement, access to knowledge assets and uptake of research findings

-Strategic universities and research institutions in the region have a clear program in place and access to resources to support female researchers of forest landscape governance and to strengthen the quality of research of gender issues related to forest landscape governance</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet &quot;Strengthening Science-Policy Interface and Universities&#x2019; Research Capacities for Forest Landscape Governance in Southeast Asia: Explore Phase 2&quot;&#xA0;ligger i linje med&#xA0;Strategi f&#xF6;r Sveriges regionala utvecklingssamarbete med Asien och Oceanien 2022-2026&#xA0;och&#xA0;Strategi f&#xF6;r Sveriges utvecklingssamarbete inom forskning f&#xF6;r fattigdomsbek&#xE4;mpning och h&#xE5;llbar utveckling 2022-2026. Projektet genomf&#xF6;rs p&#xE5; lokal, nationell och regional niv&#xE5;, med s&#xE4;rskilt fokus p&#xE5; universitet och forskare i Kambodja, Indonesien, Laos, Myanmar, Filippinerna, Thailand, Timor Lest&#xE9; och Vietnam.

Projektet bidrar till f&#xF6;ljande specifika prioriteringar i&#xA0;Strategin f&#xF6;r forskningssamarbete och forskning i utveckling:

- St&#xE4;rkt forskningskapacitet och h&#xE5;llbara forskningsmilj&#xF6;er. Projektet kommer att st&#xE4;rka forskningskapaciteten vid universitet i &#xE5;tta l&#xE4;nder genom forskningsbidrag, n&#xE4;tverksm&#xF6;ten, seminarier, j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhetsprojekt inom universitet, och vetenskapligt mentorskap.

- St&#xE4;rkt global, regional och nationell forskning av relevans f&#xF6;r minst utvecklade l&#xE4;nder och regioner. Projektet kommer att leda till mer regional forskning om relationen mellan skogsbruk och j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet, klimatf&#xF6;r&#xE4;ndringar, milj&#xF6;, biodiversitet, m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter, fattigdomsbek&#xE4;mpning och &#xE5;terh&#xE4;mtning fr&#xE5;n covid-19 pandemin.

- St&#xE4;rkt genomslag f&#xF6;r forskning av relevans f&#xF6;r fattigdomsbek&#xE4;mpning och h&#xE5;llbar utveckling. Projektets fokus p&#xE5; deltagarinriktad och insatsbaserad forksning kommer att &#xF6;ka forskarnas f&#xF6;rm&#xE5;ga att samarbeta och samverka med beslutsfattare, utvecklingsakt&#xF6;rer, skogsbrukare och samh&#xE4;llsmedlemmar. Detta kommer att leda till en samproducerad kunskapsproduktion som har l&#xE5;ngsiktiga positiva effekter f&#xF6;r marginaliserade och utsatta grupper.

Projektet kompletterar Sveriges strategi f&#xF6;r regionala utvecklingssamarbeten i Asien och Oceanien genom att bidra till h&#xE5;llbar utveckling i skogsomr&#xE5;den i Sydostasien. Projektets metod integrerar m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet samt inkluderar marginaliserade grupper och grupper som lever i fattigdom. Svenskt st&#xF6;d till projektet kommer att resultera i nya akt&#xF6;rer (sekretariatet, n&#xE4;tverket och forskningsgrupperna) som kan arbeta regionalt i Sydostasien f&#xF6;r att hantera nationella och gr&#xE4;ns&#xF6;verskridande utmaningar relaterade till skog, skogsbruk, och skogsf&#xF6;rvaltning. Projektet samarbetar ocks&#xE5; med befintliga institutioner och organisationer som universitet, organisationer i civilsamh&#xE4;llet, myndigheter och ASEAN. Initiativets f&#xF6;reslagna arbetsmetod motsvarar Sveriges egen prioritering av integrerade strategier vilka underl&#xE4;ttar kommunikation och samarbete mellan civilsamh&#xE4;llet, myndigheter, privata f&#xF6;retag och forskning. Samtidigt st&#xF6;djer projektet dessa akt&#xF6;rers f&#xF6;rm&#xE5;ga att bidra till utvecklingen av oberoende arenor f&#xF6;r informationsspridning, n&#xE4;tverkande och ansvarsutkr&#xE4;vande i relation till m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och fr&#xE4;mjandet av en milj&#xF6;m&#xE4;ssigt h&#xE5;llbar utveckling i Sydostasen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Strengthening Science-Policy Interface and Universities&#x2019; Research Capacities for Forest Landscape Governance in Southeast Asia: Explore Phase 2&quot; is aligned with the Strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s Regional Development Cooperation with Asia and Oceania 2022-2026, and the Strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s Development Cooperation within Research for Poverty Elimination and Sustainable Development 2022-2026. The project is carried out local, national and regional levels, with special focus on universities and researchers in Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Myanmar, the Philippines, Thailand, Timor Lest&#xE9; and Vietnam.

The project contributes to the following priorities of the Strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s Development Cooperation within Research for Poverty Elimination and Sustainable Development 2022-2026:&#xA0;

- Strengthened research capacity and sustainable research environments. The project will strengthen research capacity at universities in eight countries through research grants, network meetings, seminars, gender-equality projects within universities, and mentorship.

Strengthened global, regional and national research of relevance for least developed countries and regions. The project will lead to more regional research on the relationship between forest landscape resources and gender equality, climate change, environment, biodiversity, human rights, poverty elimination, and recovery from the covid-19 pandemic.

- Strengthened&#xA0;impact of research that is relevant for poverty elimination and sustainable development. The project&apos;s focus on participatory action research will increase researchers&apos; capacity to cooperate and coordinate with decision makers, development actors, forest-users and community members. This will lead to new knowledge with long-term positive impacts for marginalized and vulnerable groups.

The project contributes to the Strategy for Sweden&#x2019;s Regional Development Cooperation with Asia and Oceania 2022-2026 by contributing to sustainable development in forest landscapes of Southeast Asia. The project&apos;s approach integrates human rights and gender equality, and it includes marginalized groups and groups that live in poverty. Sweden&apos;s support will result in new actors (e.g. the Explore Secretariat, Explore Network, and transboundary research groups) that can work regionally to address national and transboundary problems&#xA0;related to forests, forest management, and forest use. The project cooperates with already existing institutions and organizations including universities, civil society organizations, government agencies, and ASEAN. The project uses a multistakeholder approach that encourages stakeholders to contribute to free and independent exchange of knowledge, networking, and respect for human rights and environmentally sustainable development in Southeast Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
